cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the submission-aligned materials, please cite the repository and the associated manuscript when available."
title: "Hill-Enigma-SPN (HESPN): Rotor-Scheduled Hill Matrices as an SPN Mix Layer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Coggins"
    given-names: "Porter E."
    name-suffix: "III"
    affiliation: "Bemidji State University"
version: "CiC Revision 2"
date-released: "2026-08-28"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ja9925ydbsu/Hill-Enigma-SPN-HESPN-COGGINS"
license: MIT
abstract: "Research software and submission-aligned materials for evaluating whether rotor-scheduled Hill-derived 8 x 8 binary matrices can be specified and used as a reversible, locally diffusion-bounded mix layer in an experimental substitution-permutation network. HESPN is a research harness, not a deployment-ready cipher or a claimed replacement for a standardized primitive."
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - Hill cipher
  - substitution-permutation network
  - matrix diffusion
  - rotor scheduling
  - branch number
  - HESPN
